# Work Shackle core constraints

- `docs/PRD.md` is the product scope source of truth.
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` is the technical architecture source of truth.
- Implement exactly one TASK at a time.
- Do not implement features outside the current TASK.
- Do not add V1-excluded features: AI/LLM, login, cloud sync, team collaboration, telemetry, online meme APIs, mobile app.
- Do not switch the approved stack (Tauri 2 + React + TypeScript + Rust + rusqlite) without explicit user approval.
- Do not perform unrelated refactors while completing a feature.
- Preserve existing user data. Never solve a migration problem by deleting or recreating the user's database.
- If the requested change requires more than 8 major files or crosses unrelated features, stop and propose a smaller split before editing.
- Read the current TASK first. Read only the PRD sections and source directories needed for that TASK.
- After implementation, run the smallest relevant tests and report only: changed files, implementation, tests run, unresolved issues.
